⚡ 1. Operators in Java

Operators are symbols used to **perform operations on variables and values**.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Types of Operators

---

🔹 1. Arithmetic Operators

| Operator | Meaning        | Example |
| -------- | -------------- | ------- |
| +        | Addition       | a + b   |
| -        | Subtraction    | a - b   |
| *        | Multiplication | a * b   |
| /        | Division       | a / b   |
| %        | Modulus        | a % b   |

---

📌 Example

```java id="op1"
int a = 10, b = 3;
System.out.println(a + b); // 13
System.out.println(a % b); // 1
```

---

🔹 2. Relational Operators

| Operator | Meaning       |
| -------- | ------------- |
| ==       | Equal to      |
| !=       | Not equal     |
| >        | Greater than  |
| <        | Less than     |
| >=       | Greater equal |
| <=       | Less equal    |

---

📌 Example

```java id="op2"
System.out.println(10 > 5);  // true
System.out.println(10 == 5); // false
```

---

🔹 3. Logical Operators

| Operator | Meaning |
| -------- | ------- |
| &&       | AND     |
| ||       | OR      |
| !        | NOT     |

---

📌 Example

```java id="op3"
boolean x = true, y = false;
System.out.println(x && y); // false
System.out.println(x || y); // true
```

---

🔹 4. Assignment Operators

| Operator | Example |
| -------- | ------- |
| =        | a = 10  |
| +=       | a += 5  |
| -=       | a -= 5  |
| *=       | a *= 2  |
| /=       | a /= 2  |

---

🔹 5. Increment / Decrement

| Operator | Meaning       |
| -------- | ------------- |
| ++       | Increase by 1 |
| --       | Decrease by 1 |

---

📌 Example

```java id="op4"
int x = 5;
x++;
System.out.println(x); // 6
```

